<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lodi Vecchio</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Laus Pompeia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> Vecchio is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> on the site of Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laus">Laus</a> Pompeia and of medieval Lodi. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> destroyed the old city in 1111 and again in 1158, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> refounded Lodi on a new site on the Adda a few miles away. The old site survived as a village, keeping the Romanesque basilica of San Bassiano.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lodi-vecchio.jpg" alt="Lodi Vecchio" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kiban · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lodi_Vecchio-Chiesa_san_Bassiano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
